- heading "Web Scraping Sandbox" [level=1]
- separator
- 'heading "Countries of the World: A Simple Example" [level=3]':
  - 'link "Countries of the World: A Simple Example"':
    - /url: /pages/simple/
- paragraph: A single page that lists information about all the countries in the world. Good for those just get started with web scraping.
- separator
- 'heading "Hockey Teams: Forms, Searching and Pagination" [level=3]':
  - 'link "Hockey Teams: Forms, Searching and Pagination"':
    - /url: /pages/forms/
- paragraph: Browse through a database of NHL team stats since 1990. Practice building a scraper that handles common website interface components.
- separator
- 'heading "Oscar Winning Films: AJAX and Javascript" [level=3]':
  - 'link "Oscar Winning Films: AJAX and Javascript"':
    - /url: /pages/ajax-javascript/
- paragraph: Click through a bunch of great films. Learn how content is added to the page asynchronously with Javascript and how you can scrape it.
- separator
- 'heading "Turtles All the Way Down: Frames & iFrames" [level=3]':
  - 'link "Turtles All the Way Down: Frames & iFrames"':
    - /url: /pages/frames/
- paragraph: Some older sites might still use frames to break up thier pages. Modern ones might be using iFrames to expose data. Learn about turtles as you scrape content inside frames.
- separator
- 'heading "Advanced Topics: Real World Challenges You''ll Encounter" [level=3]':
  - 'link "Advanced Topics: Real World Challenges You''ll Encounter"':
    - /url: /pages/advanced/
- paragraph: Scraping real websites, you're likely run into a number of common gotchas. Get practice with spoofing headers, handling logins & session cookies, finding CSRF tokens, and other common network errors.
- separator
- text: Lessons and Videos © Hartley Brody 2023